# Build-context exclusions, shared by EVERY build path — the podman drill
# (safe_agents/arms/local/container-arc-run.sh), the CI container-arc job, the
# OpenShift BuildConfigs (safe_agents/arms/openshift/), and a consumer agent's
# own image build. ONE context definition on purpose: a per-path exclusion
# list is how the cluster and the laptop end up disagreeing about an image that
# has the same name in both places.
#
# Nothing listed here is COPYed by any Containerfile. The base image copies
# pyproject.toml, README.md, LICENSE, safe_agents/, and one ec2 bootstrap
# script; consumer layers copy their own examples/ subdirectory.
#
# This exists because the context was 634 MB, of which ~570 MB was virtualenvs
# and node_modules — irrelevant to a podman build on a warm cache, fatal to a
# binary BuildConfig that uploads the context to the cluster on every build.

.git
.venv
**/.venv
infra/node_modules
infra/cdk.out
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
.coverage
